main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assignment operator template defined: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
Among the out-of-class definitions of same-named member templates, the one
with the most template parameters was preferred before the owning class
was compared, so another class template's operator= hid fn's own
definition and fn<int>::operator=<F> had no body.  libc++'s
std::unordered_multimap::operator= hid that of std::function.
